<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apollo Grannus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> Grannus was a Gallo-Roman healing god, the Celtic deity Grannus identified with the Roman Apollo and worshipped especially at springs. His cult was strong in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a>, and his greatest sanctuary was at Grand in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>, where a large mosaic and an amphitheatre survive. The emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracalla">Caracalla</a> sought a cure at a shrine of Grannus in 213 CE.</p></div>
